<p>U.S. Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee triggered a wave of diplomatic backlash after remarks in an interview with conservative commentator Tucker Carlson were widely read as endorsing Israeli control over a broad swath of the Middle East. Arab leaders and a coalition of Arab and Islamic governments condemned the comments as dangerous, saying they could threaten regional stability. Huckabee and the U.S. Embassy in Jerusalem said his remarks were taken out of context and rejected the interpretation that he was urging territorial expansion. The episode has renewed attention on how quickly U.S. statements can ripple across the region—and how quickly regional organizations and governments can still coordinate a collective diplomatic response when they believe core principles are on the line.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gRwqDtwXzFMB8cBgAjMrWneFQiPLGmJm2GfGBEFbvOi20ts9Vu686KXzoEvfZ5pP0194lrs6kTY3i_DjbGbP9VJX3bQkBTSLlETWEqrIGZa2S6tiMo3kdSWi1lWTe3V17XypoXZ3wFkpWbzVvfKQ_kxaMEVZUoW0VeDa3T5ytmgR7fa1cQOCPwHBsCx3-5MVXZUosqvFBYYE-tzwsu29EjoFnclfjGxuSjFuScDW6oyyhMysAo_lNKIGxTw8tHoCp7AKx_n4tKCPit4w5w' alt='FILE - U.S. Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee poses for a photo during an interview in Jerusalem, Aug. 20, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Diplomatic bind: Dawn cited an international law expert who said the remarks put Washington in a bind, arguing a diplomat should not endorse what could be seen as “aggressive actions”.</li><li>Two-state worries: Dawn reported that many in the Arab world read the remarks as a sign of wavering U.S. support for a two-state solution.</li><li>Rights warning: Al Jazeera reported that a rights advocate said failing to remove Huckabee would be seen worldwide as President Trump endorsing those views.</li><li>How it spread: Huckabee made the comments in a Tucker Carlson interview that aired Friday, and regional condemnations followed soon after.</li><li>Messenger matters: The Guardian noted that Huckabee—an evangelical Christian pastor and former Arkansas governor—has long backed Israeli settlements, shaping how listeners received his remarks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Embassy in Jerusalem: The embassy said Huckabee’s remarks were taken out of context and rejected the interpretation that he called for Israeli expansion into neighboring states. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/mike-huckabee-israel-middle-east-arab-muslim-countries-comments/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Arab and Islamic governments (joint statement): A coalition of 14 governments, along with the OIC, Arab League and GCC, issued a joint condemnation expressing “strong condemnation and profound concern” over Huckabee’s remarks. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975098/us-envoys-remarks-rile-up-nations-from-nile-to-euphrates-and-beyond'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Arab leaders: Arab leaders condemned the remarks after many interpreted them as endorsing Israeli control of territory stretching from Egypt toward Iraq, according to the New York Times. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/middleeast/huckabee-israel-tucker-carlson.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Rights advocates: A rights advocate warned that keeping Huckabee in the post would be read as President Trump endorsing his views, Al Jazeera reported. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/us-envoy-huckabee-tries-to-deny-saying-he-would-support-israel-expansionism'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Huckabee: In the Tucker Carlson interview, Huckabee’s comments were widely interpreted as suggesting Israel could legitimately claim a broad swath of the region; after the backlash, he said the remarks were taken out of context. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-says-ambassadors-comments-on-israel-middle-east-taken-out-of/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/mike-huckabee-israel-middle-east-arab-muslim-countries-comments/'>Huckabee&#x27;s remarks on Israel and Middle East were taken out of context, embassy says</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-says-ambassadors-comments-on-israel-middle-east-taken-out-of/'>U.S. says ambassador’s comments on Israel, Middle East taken out of context</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/middleeast/huckabee-israel-tucker-carlson.html'>Arab Leaders Condemn Remarks by U.S. Ambassador to Israel</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/us-envoy-huckabee-tries-to-deny-saying-he-would-support-israel-expansionism'>US envoy Huckabee tries to deny saying he would support Israel expansionism</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/22/mike-huckabee-israel-comments-condemned-arab-muslim-countries'>Huckabee’s Israel land remarks condemned as ‘dangerous and inflammatory’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975098/us-envoys-remarks-rile-up-nations-from-nile-to-euphrates-and-beyond'>US envoy’s remarks rile up nations ‘from Nile to Euphrates’ and beyond</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>